    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n40 Dargan Street is a stunning two-bedroom mid-terraced period home, presented in immaculate turnkey condition and finished to an exceptional standard throughout. Behind its charming façade lies a beautifully calm and thoughtfully designed interior, filled with natural light and perfectly suited to first-time buyers, downsizers, or those seeking a stylish home in a convenient setting.\n\nUpon entering, you are welcomed directly into a bright and inviting living room, complete with a feature open fireplace, the ideal setting for cosy evenings at home. To the rear, a recently upgraded kitchen offers ample storage and generous workspace, combining practicality with contemporary style.\n\nBeyond the kitchen, a rear hallway leads to a well-appointed family bathroom featuring a fitted bath with overhead shower, wash hand basin (WHB), WC, and excellent storage solutions. The bathroom is also conveniently plumbed for both a washing machine and dryer.\n\nUpstairs, the accommodation comprises two spacious double bedrooms, each beautifully styled and finished to a high standard, creating warm and comfortable retreats.\n\nExternally, a private rear courtyard provides a low-maintenance outdoor space, completing this charming home. On-street resident parking is available.\n\nPerfectly positioned in the heart of Bray, the property enjoys all the benefits of town-centre living, with Main Street and Castle Street Shopping Centre just a short stroll away. Bray is a vibrant and thriving seaside town offering an excellent selection of shops, cafés, restaurants, bars, local businesses, and cultural amenities, including the renowned Mermaid Arts Centre.\n\nThe entrance to the picturesque riverside People's Park and boardwalk is just 250 metres from the property — a wonderful local amenity for residents to enjoy. Bray's famous mile-long Victorian promenade, framed by Bray Head, is approximately 1km away and can be accessed through the town or via a scenic pedestrian riverside path through the harbour. Here, residents can enjoy leisurely seaside walks, a children's playground, popular restaurants, trendy cafés and bars, and charming ice cream parlours.\n\nThe area also benefits from an excellent choice of highly regarded primary and secondary schools, alongside a wide range of sporting and leisure facilities. For commuters, multiple bus routes service nearby Castle Street, just 300 metres from the property, while the DART station is within comfortable walking distance. The N11/M11/M50 corridor is also easily accessible, ensuring excellent connectivity to Dublin and beyond.\n\nKey points: \n\n• 40 Dargan Street is a beautifully presented 2-bedroom mid-terraced period home in turnkey condition\n• Bright, calm interior with high-quality finishes throughout\n• Upgraded PVC Triple glaze windows and doors.\n• Living room with feature open fireplace\n• Recently upgraded kitchen with ample storage\n• Ground floor bathroom with bath/shower, WHB, WC, storage, plus plumbing for washer/dryer\n• Two spacious and well-styled double bedrooms upstairs\n• Private rear courtyard and on-street resident parking\n• Central Bray location, minutes from Main Street and Castle Street Shopping Centre\n• 250m to People's Park and riverside boardwalk\n• 1km to Bray seafront promenade and Bray Head walks\n• Wide range of cafés, restaurants, shops, and amenities nearby\n• Excellent schools and leisure facilities in the area\n• Strong transport links: bus routes nearby, walking distance to DART, and easy access to N11/M11/M50"
      },
